# waynergy raw-keymap: macOS Barrier/Synergy server -> Linux (xkb evdev) client
#
# Keys are the keycodes sent by the macOS server; values are the local
# xkb/evdev keycodes to emit.  The macOS server keycodes correspond to the
# values in doc/xkb/keycodes/mac minus 7 (that file encodes mac keycode + 8,
# while the server sends mac keycode + 1).
#
# Keep xkb_key_offset = 0 and do NOT point xkb_keymap at the mac keycodes:
# upload a normal evdev keymap (e.g. the compositor default, or
# doc/config-example/xkb_keymap) so that modifier keys (Command, Option ->
# Super/Alt) are applied correctly.  Then include this section in config.ini.
#
# Generated from doc/xkb/keycodes/mac and xkb-config's evdev keycodes.

